 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to granting the Nyack joint fire district local development corporation and the Nyack general fire protection company, Inc. legal corporate status as not-for-profit corporations",
    "basePrintNo": "S7690",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7690-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Rockland County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7690\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to granting the Nyack joint fire\ndistrict local development corporation and the Nyack general fire\nprotection company, Inc. legal corporate status as not-for-profit\ncorporations\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would grant legal corporate status as not-for-profit\ncorporations pursuant to section 1411 of the New York State\nNot-for-Profit Corporation Law to the Nyack Joint Fire District Local\nDevelopment Corporation and the Nyack General Fire Protection Company,\nInc., to authorize the transfer of title to the Park Street fire\nstation from the Nyack General Fire Protection Company, Inc. to the\nNyack Joint Fire District, in the Towns of Orangetown and Clarkstown\nand the Villages of Nyack, Upper Nyack, South Nyack and Upper\nGrandview in Rockland County (the \"Nyack Joint Fire District\").  In\naddition, this bill will legalize, validate and confirm certain prior\nactions by the Nyack LDCs, which were the subject of a critical report\nprepared by the Office of the State Comptroller in December, 2009.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. (i) Grants legal corporate status to the Nyack Joint Fire\nDistrict Local Development Corporation and the Nyack General fire\nProtection Company, Inc. (collectively, the Nyack LDCs\"), as\nnot-for-profit corporations pursuant to section 1411 of the\nNot-for-Profit Corporation Law, with the same rights powers and\nprivileges of any corporation heretofore or hereafter incorporated\nunder such section; (ii) legalizes, validates and confirms the\ntransfer of several parcels of real property located on Park Street in\nthe Village of Nyack and currently the site of the Park Street fire\nstation from the Nyack Joint Fire District Local Development\nCorporation to the Nyack General Fire Protection Company, Inc. and the\nlease between the Nyack General Fire Protection Company, Inc. to the\nNyack Joint Fire District, in the Towns of Orangetown and Clarkstown\nand the Villages of Nyack, Upper Nyack, South Nyack and Upper\nGrandview in Rockland County (the \"Nyack Joint Fire District\"); (iii)\nauthorizes the sale of such parcels of real property by the Nyack\nGeneral fire Protection Company, Inc. to the Nyack Joint Fire\nDistrict, upon such terms and conditions and for such consideration as\nmay be agreed upon; (iv) terminates the corporate existence of the\nNyack LDCs upon such sale or conveyance and the satisfaction of all\ndebts, obligations and liabilities by the Nyack LDCs and (v) passes to\nand vests in the Nyack Joint Fire District all of the rights and\nproperties of the Nyack LDC then remaining.\n\nSection 2. Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Nyack Joint Fire District presently leases a fire station located\non Park Street in the Village of Nyack from the Nyack General fire\nProtection Company, Inc., a local development corporation. The Board\nof Fire Commissioners has determined that there are significant\nfinancial benefits to the taxpayers if the Nyack Joint Fire District\n\n\nissues bonds to acquire the fire station and terminates the lease. In\nfurtherance thereof, in December 2013, a proposition was approved by a\nmajority of the voters of the Nyack Joint Fire District authorizing\nthe issuance of bonds not to exceed $3,000,000 by the Nyack Joint Fire\nDistrict to finance the acquisition of the fire station located on\nPark Street. In order to assure the validity of the transfer of title\nfrom the Nyack General Fire Protection Company, Inc. to the Nyack\nJoint Fire District and to resolve any other questions surrounding the\nlegality of the actions taken by the Nyack General Fire Protection\nCompany, Inc. and a second local development corporation formed for\nthe express purpose of financing the construction of said fire\nstation, the Nyack Joint Fire District is seeking this validating act.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
