    "lawSection": "Rockland County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7690A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to granting the Nyack joint fire\ndistrict local development corporation and the Nyack general fire\nprotection company, Inc. legal corporate status as not-for-profit\ncorporations\n\nPURPOSE:  This bill would grant legal corporate status as\nnot-for-profit corporations pursuant to the New York State\nnot-for-profit corporation law to the Nyack Joint Fire District Local\nDevelopment Corporation (the \"LDC\") and the Nyack General Fire\nProtection Company, Inc. (the \"Fire Co.\") and to authorize the valid\nand legal transfer of title to the Park Street fire station from the\nFire Co.  to the Nyack Joint Fire District, in the Towns of Orangetown\nand Clarkstown and the Villages of Nyack, Upper Nyack, South Nyack and\nUpper Grandview in Rockland County (the \"Nyack Joint Fire District\").\nIn addition, this act will address and remedy certain prior actions by\nthe LDC and the Fire Co., which were the subject of a report prepared\nby the Office of the State Comptroller in December, 2009.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. (i) Grants legal corporate status to the Nyack Joint Fire\nDistrict Local Development Corporation and the Nyack General Fire\nProtection Company, Inc., as not-for-profit corporations pursuant to\nthe New York State not-for-profit corporation law; (ii) legalizes,\nvalidates, ratifies and confirms the transfer of several parcels of\nreal property located on Park Street in the Village of Nyack and\ncurrently the site of the Park Street fire station from the LDC to the\nFire Co. and the lease between the Fire Co. to the Nyack Joint Fire\nDistrict; and (iii) authorizes the sale, without judicial\nintervention, of such parcels of real property by the Fire Co. to the\nNyack Joint Fire District, upon such terms and conditions and for such\nconsideration as have been agreed upon.\n\nSection 2. Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  The Nyack Joint Fire District presently leases a fire\nstation located on Park Street in the Village of Nyack from the Nyack\nGeneral Fire Protection Company, Inc. The lease by and between the\nNyack General Fire Protection Company, Inc. and the Nyack Joint Fire\nDistrict provides an option to purchase, at any time during the term\nof the lease, for a sum of one dollar ($1.00), plus payment of any and\nall mortgages, liens or other encumbrances of record against the\nproperty. The Board of Fire Commissioners has determined that there\nwill be significant financial benefits to the taxpayers of the Nyack\nJoint Fire District if the Nyack Joint Fire District exercises the\npurchase option set forth in the lease because the debt service cost\non bonds issued by the Nyack Joint Fire District to acquire the fire\nstation will be substantially lower than the lease payments required\nto be made by the Nyack Joint Fire District pursuant to the terms of\nthe lease. In furtherance thereof, in December 2013, a proposition for\napproval of a bond resolution was approved by a majority of the voters\nof the Nyack Joint Fire District authorizing the issuance of not to\nexceed $3 million in bonds of the Nyack Joint Fire District to finance\nthe acquisition of the fire station located on Park Street.\n\n\nIn order (i) to assure the validity of the transfer of title from the\nFire Co. to the Nyack Joint Fire District, (ii) to resolve any other\nquestions surrounding the legality of the actions taken by the LDC and\nthe Fire Co., formed for the express purpose of financing the\nconstruction of said fire station, and (iii) to eliminate the need for\njudicial intervention for said transfer of title, the Nyack Joint Fire\nDistrict is seeking this special act.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
